{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Day With Vanessa"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Last Minute Cancellation"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouncing the Suffix -tion"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Suffixes are parts of words that are at the end. They often indicate the form of the word."}, {"type": "text", "content": " One of the most common suffixes is <span class=\"italic\">-tion</span>. This indicates that the word is a noun."}, {"type": "text", "content": " For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " To reserve - Reserva<span class=\"strong\">tion</span><br/>To compete - Competi<span class=\"strong\">tion</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " The suffix <span class=\"italic\">-tion</span> is pronounced with a /sh/ sound and a schwa. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " You stress the syllable that comes right before the suffix."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Say these words. Stress the bolded syllable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br/>reser<span class=\"strong\">va</span>tion<br/>compe<span class=\"strong\">ti</span>tion<br/>re<span class=\"strong\">a</span>ction<br/>cancel<span class=\"strong\">la</span>tion<br/>att<span class=\"strong\">en</span>tion<br/>introd<span class=\"strong\">uc</span>tion<br/>sani<span class=\"strong\">ta</span>tion<br/><span class=\"strong\">op</span>tion"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I made reservations at the restaurant next to the art gallery. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm a little worried about my bistro - there's so much more competition!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Look, there's a new exhibition coming next month! "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing New Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In conversation, it is not always WHAT you say but HOW you say it. You can use stress to introduce new information and to show that you are listening and understand other people's feelings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Usually, the stressed words in a sentence are the nouns, verbs, adjectives and adverbs. <br/>Sometimes, you can choose to stress other types of words to show that you are adding new information or showing that you understand other people's feelings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm famished after all that walking! I feel like a bowl of pasta!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: A <span class=\"strong\">giant</span> bowl of pasta! I'm starving, too! </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this case, Sally stresses <span class=\"strong\">giant</span>. She is adding new information to the idea of a bowl of pasta and she is showing that she understands Vanessa's feeling of being hungry."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can stress words like <span class=\"italic\">really</span> when you want to show empathy. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">That's got to be <span class=\"strong\">really</span> worrying!</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Look, there's a new exhibition coming next month! We have to go!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: <span class=\"underline\">Which</span> exhibition? "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "famished"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very hungry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm famished after all that walking! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about social activities."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pop up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to suddenly appear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are more restaurants popping up in this neighborhood lately."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le16ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": 